# Schema: Micro-Unit

Spec: Schema

ID:
  @micro-unit

Purpose:
  Machine-readable schema for the MICRO-UNIT entity — the smallest
  parallel-executable unit of the SW1 swarm pipeline (bax
  ../workflow/micro-unit.sdd). Extends schemas/subtask.sdd with the
  hard D2 budget and the swarm lifecycle.

Owns: schemas/micro-unit.sdd

Schema:

  mu_id: MU-<STAGE>-<NN>
      example: MU-BE-03

  stage: <SW1 stage key>
      The owning macro-stage.

  goal: <one line>

  budget:
    files: 1
    line_diff: 150
    token_pack: 8000
    subagent_step: 1
      HARD caps (D2). A unit exceeding ANY cap is recursively
      subdivided before dispatch.

  scope:
    allowed: [<paths>]
    allowed_actions: [code | tests | docs | config | refactor | research]
    forbidden: [<prohibitions>]

  depends_on: [MU-<id>]

  parallelism:
    parallel_ready: true | false
    shared_state: <none | [locked resources]>

  channel: R | F
      Dispatch channel (bax ../workflow/dispatch-channels.sdd).
      Derived: F iff parallel_ready && shared_state == none,
      else R. Never set manually ([DC1]).

  parent_agent: <agent id | none>
      Spawning agent (L1) that owns this unit; none for
      supervisor-decomposed units.

  child_agents: [<agent ids>]
      L2 sub-agents spawned by self-delegation ([SAL2]);
      depth cap 2 ([SAL1]).

  folder: <runtime path | none>
      .specdd/swarm/{run_id}/agents/{agent_id}/ — context
      pack + outcome + evidence ([SAL5]).

  impact:
    blast_radius: LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL
    affected: [<layers>]
    review_route: <derived>

  lifecycle:
    TODO -> DISPATCHED -> IMPLEMENTING -> MERGED -> VERIFIED -> DONE
    defect path: -> DEFECTED -> FOCUS -> VERIFIED -> DONE

  agent:
    assigned: <subagent id | none>
    token_used: <int>

  done_proof:
    artifact: <file(s)>
    validation: <test run | review id | scan id; NEVER "looks correct">

  defect:
    defect_id: DEF-<id> | none
    focus_iterations: <int>
      Attribution record: which defect triggered a FOCUS cycle on this
      unit, and how many focus iterations it took.

Rules:

  [MS1] mu_id MUST be unique and stable across the run lifetime.
  [MS2] goal MUST be a single objective — split otherwise.
  [MS3] budget caps are HARD; subdivision is the only remedy.
  [MS4] forbidden MUST be explicit — empty requires
        "forbidden: none (scoped to allowed only)".
  [MS5] lifecycle transitions follow the swarm state machine; no
        direct TODO -> DONE.
  [MS6] done_proof MUST exist before DONE (bax ../tasks/DONE-PROOF.sdd).
  [MS7] defect.defect_id is set when the unit enters DEFECTED; each
        FOCUS iteration increments focus_iterations.
  [MS8] impact.blast_radius MUST be set before TODO leaves (bax
        ../schemas/subtask.sdd [SB8]); CRITICAL blocks auto-merge.
  [MS9] channel MUST be derived per dispatch-channels.sdd [DC1] —
        manual assignment is a SPEC VIOLATION.
  [MS10] parent_agent/child_agents MUST form a tree of depth
        <= 2 ([SAL1]); children are recorded at spawn time.
  [MS11] folder MUST be under .specdd/swarm/{run_id}/agents/
        and is deleted per [SAL6] after DONE + VERIFIED.

Templates:
  Runtime instances live in .specdd/swarm/{run_id}/micro_units/
  (never committed, [R103]).

Navigation:
  MicroUnitEntity: @../workflow/micro-unit.sdd
  SubtaskSchema: @subtask.sdd
  SwarmChain: @../chains/swarm.sdd
  DispatchChannels: @../workflow/dispatch-channels.sdd
  SubagentLifecycle: @../agent/subagent-lifecycle.sdd

State: +
  (Phase 160 — schema for the D2-sized parallel unit; extends
   subtask.sdd with budget, parallelism, defect, and agent fields)
  (Phase 161 — added channel, parent_agent, child_agents, folder
   fields + [MS9]-[MS11] per DEC-2026-1011-002)